{"id":"og","name":"Og","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:og"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Og","text":"Gigantic, the king of Bashan, who was defeated by Moses in a pitched battle at Edrei, and was slain along with his sons (Deut. 1:4), and whose kingdom was given to the tribes of Reuben and Gad and half the tribe of Manasseh (Num. 21:32-35; Deut. 3:1-13). His bedstead (or rather sarcophagus) was of iron (or ironstone), 9 cubits in length and 4 cubits in breadth. His overthrow was afterwards celebrated in song (Ps. 135:11; 136:20). (See SIHON.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5747","lemma":"עוֹג","xlit":"ʻÔwg","gloss":"Og, a king of Bashan","kjv":"Og","count":22,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H1316","lemma":"בָּשָׁן","xlit":"Bâshân","gloss":"Bashan , a region East of the Jordan","kjv":"Bashan","count":22,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H5511","lemma":"סִיחוֹן","xlit":"Çîychôwn","gloss":"Sichon, an Amoritish king","kjv":"Sihon","count":14,"share":0.32},{"strong":"H567","lemma":"אֱמֹרִי","xlit":"ʼĔmôrîy","gloss":"an Emorite, one of the Canaanitish tribes","kjv":"Amorite","count":13,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H154","lemma":"אֶדְרֶעִי","xlit":"ʼedreʻîy","gloss":"Edrei, the name of two places in Palestine","kjv":"Edrei","count":7,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H2809","lemma":"חֶשְׁבּוֹן","xlit":"Cheshbôwn","gloss":"Cheshbon, a place East of the Jordan","kjv":"Heshbon","count":8,"share":0.18}],"verses":["Num.21.33","Num.32.33","Deut.1.4","Deut.3.1","Deut.3.3","Deut.3.4","Deut.3.10","Deut.3.11","Deut.3.13","Deut.4.47","Deut.29.7","Deut.31.4","Josh.2.10","Josh.9.10","Josh.12.4","Josh.13.12","Josh.13.30","Josh.13.31","1Kgs.4.19","Neh.9.22","Ps.135.11","Ps.136.20","Num.21.34","Num.21.35","Deut.3.2","Deut.3.5","Deut.3.6","Deut.3.7","Deut.3.8","Deut.3.9","Deut.3.12","Deut.3.14","Deut.3.15","Deut.3.16","Deut.3.17","Deut.4.48","Deut.4.49","Deut.29.8","Josh.12.5","Josh.12.6","Ps.135.10","Ps.136.18","Ps.136.19","Ps.136.21"],"related":[{"id":"bashan","type":"cooccur","s